# Stories Route

Route: `/stories` (listing), `/stories/[slug]` (single story)

## Purpose

Nail community interviews/features. Two-way conversation format — a Mirellé
author writes the piece, but it's typically built around a **featured**
person (the nail artist/tech being interviewed) who gets their own credit
section.

## Files

```
src/app/stories/page.tsx              — listing page (grid, pagination, category filter)
src/app/stories/[slug]/page.tsx       — single story page
src/lib/stories.ts                    — markdown loader + query helpers
src/types/stories.ts                  — Story, StoryBodyImage, StoryFeaturedPerson types
src/components/Stories/
  StoriesGrid.tsx                     — card grid (listing page)
  StoryFeatured.tsx                   — featured/interviewee card
  StoryAbout.tsx                      — "About Mirellé" section
  StoryFinalNewsletter.tsx            — end-of-page newsletter signup
  StoryInlineNewsletter.tsx           — thin banner variant (not used by
                                          default — SocialFollowCTA is used
                                          at the 50% body break instead)
  StoryReadMore.tsx                   — related stories grid, up to 9
src/content/stories/*.md              — story content files
```

Content type is plain **Markdown** (`.md`), not MDX — no JSX inside content.

## Content file format

```yaml
---
title: "Story title"
excerpt: "One-line summary for cards/meta"
date: "2026-08-01"
author: "author-slug"                 # must match a slug in src/data/authors.ts
category: "Nail Stories"
image: "/images/stories/hero.jpg"     # hero, 16:9 (1200x675 min, Discover spec)
imageAlt: "Alt text for hero"
creditBodyImages: true                # master on/off switch for all body image credit lines
readTime: 6
canonical: "https://mirelleinspo.com/stories/slug"
tags: ["tag1", "tag2"]

bodyImages:                           # optional, images placed inside the article body
  - src: "/images/stories/img1.jpg"
    alt: "Alt text"
    creditSocialLink: "https://instagram.com/handle"   # optional
    creditDisplayText: "Photo: @handle"                # optional — if omitted, no credit line renders
    afterHeading: 0                    # renders after the Nth <h2> (0 = before the first h2, i.e. right after the intro)

featured:                             # optional — the interviewee/source, shown above AuthorCard
  name: "Person Name"
  image: "/images/stories/person.jpg"
  bio: "Short bio / role"
  social: "https://instagram.com/handle"   # optional
---

Article body in plain markdown. Use `## Heading` for section breaks —
bodyImages and the SocialFollowCTA break are positioned relative to these
h2 boundaries.
```

## Page layout (top to bottom)

1. Breadcrumbs — Home / Stories / [title]
2. Category label
3. H1 title
4. Byline — author + date
5. Hero image (16:9, left-aligned with title, can extend wider than the text column)
6. Article body — markdown content, with:
   - body images (from `bodyImages` frontmatter) inserted after their specified heading
   - `SocialFollowCTA` inserted automatically at the halfway point of the article
7. `StoryFeatured` — only renders if `featured` is set in frontmatter
8. `AuthorCard` — only renders if `author` slug resolves
9. `StoryAbout`
10. `StoryFinalNewsletter`
11. `StoryReadMore` — up to 9 related stories (same category first, then others)

## Layout notes

- Title/byline/body/AuthorCard column: max-width `800px`
- Hero image: max-width `1000px`, left-aligned to the same edge as the title (not centered independently)
- Body images: max-width `560px`, centered within the text column, `4:5` aspect on mobile / `3:4` on larger screens — intentionally narrower than both hero and text column width
- All widths responsive; no fixed pixel widths outside these max-widths

## Known dependencies (not part of this route, must already exist)

- `@/lib/authors` → `getAuthor(slug)`
- `@/components/Breadcrumbs`
- `@/components/Blog/AuthorCard`
- `@/components/ui/SocialFollowCTA`
- `remark`, `remark-gfm`, `remark-html`, `gray-matter` (npm packages)

## Open items / assumptions

- `StoryReadMore` groups by exact `category` string match — categories should be entered consistently across story files.
- No pagination inside a single story; `StoryReadMore` caps at 9 regardless of how many related stories exist.
- `creditBodyImages: false` in frontmatter suppresses all credit lines for that story, even if individual `bodyImages` entries have `creditDisplayText` set.
